# Logging configuration
LOG_LEVEL="info"

# ===========================================
# Security Configuration Notes
# ===========================================

# ✅ SAFE TO COMMIT:
# - Public RPC endpoints
# - Contract addresses (public on blockchain)
# - Configuration flags
# - Public API endpoints

# 🚨 NEVER COMMIT:
# - DEVELOPER_MNEMONIC (contains private keys)
# - API keys and secrets
# - TURN server credentials
# - Database passwords
# - Private keys of any kind

# 📝 CONFIGURATION VALIDATION:
# Run `npm run validate` to check environment setup
# Missing required variables will be reported

# 🔒 SECURITY BEST PRACTICES:
# 1. Use different mnemonics for development vs testnet vs mainnet
# 2. Rotate API keys regularly
# 3. Use environment-specific .env files
# 4. Never include .env in Docker images
# 5. Use secrets management in production (not .env files)

# ===========================================
# Quick Setup Guide
# ===========================================

# 1. Copy this file to .env
# 2. Replace all "your_*_here" placeholders with real values
# 3. Generate a new mnemonic for DEVELOPER_MNEMONIC (use a wallet app)
# 4. Get Filebase API key from filebase.com (free tier available)
# 5. Get TURN credentials from metered.ca (free tier available)
# 6. Run `npm run validate` to verify configuration
# 7. Run `npm run dev` to start development server

